A.R.G.U.S.

Asset Readiness & Gear Utility System

Master Product Specification

Product status: Development / Prototype
Primary organization: Local NJROTC unit
Primary purpose: Replace and centralize the unit's normal Supply workflows in one specialized application.
Architecture direction: Offline-first, multi-device, BSV-native identity/audit/synchronization architecture with no conventional centralized application database if the Stage 2 proof of concept demonstrates that this can be done safely and reliably.

---

1. PRODUCT VISION

A.R.G.U.S. is a highly specialized supply-management system designed specifically around the workflows of this NJROTC unit.

It is not intended to be a generic inventory application.

The finished system should allow the Supply Department to perform the majority of its recurring work from one application, including:

- inventory management
- physical counting
- uniform issue
- uniform return
- cadet property records
- incomplete issue tracking
- bundle management
- readiness monitoring
- supply calendar
- AMI preparation
- New Cadet Orientation preparation
- BLT preparation
- Military Ball preparation
- End-of-Year inventory
- alerts
- multi-user synchronization
- offline operations
- authorization and roles
- permanent correction history
- cryptographically verifiable audit records
- BSV-backed identity and event verification

The guiding principle is:

«A.R.G.U.S. should make Supply work faster, clearer, safer, more accurate, and easier to coordinate.»

