8. EDITABLE BUNDLE SYSTEM

Bundles must NOT be permanently hard-coded into the UI.

A.R.G.U.S. should ship with default presets but authorized users should be able to edit bundle definitions.

Bundle definitions should contain:

- bundle ID
- display name
- applicable gender if any
- applicable purpose/event
- list of items
- whether each line is required or optional
- whether the item supports sizing
- default quantity
- active/inactive state
- version/history

Changing a bundle should not silently rewrite historical transactions.

Historical issue records must preserve which bundle/version was issued at that time.

