33. IDEMPOTENCY

Every important event must have a globally unique event ID.

Processing the same event twice must not duplicate the resulting inventory mutation.

Example:

ITEM_ISSUED event ABC processed once:
Inventory 10 → 9.

Receiving event ABC again:
Inventory remains 9.

---

34. CRYPTOGRAPHIC EVENT CHAIN

Where practical, important events may reference previous accepted state/event hashes.

This can create a tamper-evident chain.

Do not assume one global previous hash works safely under concurrent offline operation.

Stage 2 must investigate an appropriate causal/versioning structure, potentially using:

- entity version
- parent event IDs
- logical clocks
- vector/causal metadata
- conflict markers

Do not implement simplistic chaining that breaks whenever two valid devices work concurrently.

