39. PRIMARY SUCCESS CRITERION

A.R.G.U.S. succeeds when the unit can realistically say:

«"Almost everything we need to do in Supply is organized and performed through A.R.G.U.S."»

It should become the single operational picture of:

WHO needs equipment

WHAT inventory exists

WHAT has been issued

WHAT has been returned

WHAT still needs attention

WHAT event is approaching

WHAT Supply needs to prepare

WHAT changed

WHO authorized the change

WHETHER all devices agree

WHETHER the important record can be independently verified

without requiring Supply personnel to understand the underlying cryptographic infrastructure.
